  "url": "https://www.sofo.org.uk/oxandbucksbridgetoofar20sept1944/",
  "title": "When the Oxf and Bucks went “A Bridge Too Far” – 20th September 1944 – Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum",
  "metaDescription": "",
  "canonical": "https://www.sofo.org.uk/oxandbucksbridgetoofar20sept1944/",
  "headings": [
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "text": "John Frost Bridge, Arnhem (Image ©Stephen Berridge)"
    },
    {
      "level": "h1",
      "text": "On this day 20th September 1944"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "text": "1ST AIRBORNE DIVISION – ARNHEM"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "text": "“Out of ammunition, God save the King”"
    },
    {
      "level": "h4",
      "text": "Last radio message from the Bridge at Arnhem."
    },
    {
      "level": "h1",
      "text": "Men of the Campaign:"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "text": "Captain Edward Alfred MOY-THOMAS - 1st Airlanding Brigade Headquarters, Staff Captain."
    },
    {
      "level": "h1",
      "text": "Men of the Campaign:"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "text": "Lieutenant John (“Jack”) Hollington GRAYBURN - 2nd Parachute Battalion. Platoon Commander, Number 2 Platoon, A Company."
    },
    {
      "level": "h4",
      "text": "Enjoyed reading this article? Please consider supporting SOFO Museum with a donation:"
    },
    {
      "level": "h4",
      "text": "Related posts"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "text": "Object of the Month: Evacuee’s Coat (Oxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects)"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "text": "Object of the Month February 2026: Sweetheart Pin Cushion"
    },
